# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file `COPY . .` ships ~1.1 GB to the Docker daemon on every
# build — almost all of it node_modules and .next, both of which are rebuilt
# inside the image anyway. Copying host node_modules in is also actively
# harmful: native modules (sharp, libvips) are compiled for the host
# architecture and would shadow the correctly-built ones from `npm ci`.

node_modules
.next
out
dist

# Local state and secrets — must never enter the image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Local tooling / editor noise
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and deploy tooling aren't needed at runtime
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
deploy.sh
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml

# Type-check artefact
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
